    metric Forms "Forms overview" "All form elements are fully responsive with pure semantic HTML, enabling forms to scale gracefully across devices and viewports."
    col
      text Content
      link Introduction /docs/forms
      link "Helper text" /docs/forms#helper-text
      link "Usage with grid" /docs/forms#usage-with-grid
      link "Usage with group" /docs/forms#usage-with-group
    col
      text Inputs are width: 100%; by default and are the same size as the buttons to build consistent forms.
      field "First name"
      field Email email
      button button primary
      link "Copy code" /docs/forms
      text "<form> <fieldset> <label> First name <input name=\"first_name\" placeholder=\"First name\" autocomplete=\"given-name\" /> </label> <label> Email <input type=\"email\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Email\" autocomplete=\"email\" /> </label> </fieldset> <input type=\"submit\" value=\"Subscribe\" /> </form>"
      text <input> can be inside or outside <label>.
      field "First name"
      text Email
      field Email email
      link "Copy code" /docs/forms
      text "<form> <!-- Input inside label --> <label> First name <input name=\"first_name\" placeholder=\"First name\" autocomplete=\"given-name\" /> </label> <!-- Input outside label --> <label for=\"email\">Email</label> <input type=\"email\" id=\"email\" placeholder=\"Email\" autocomplete=\"email\" /> </form>"
      h2 Helper text#
      text <small> below form elements are muted and act as helper texts.
      field Email email
      text We’ll never share your email with anyone else.
      link "Copy code" /docs/forms
      text "<input type=\"email\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Email\" autoComplete=\"email\" aria-label=\"Email\" aria-describedby=\"email-helper\" /> <small id=\"email-helper\"> We'll never share your email with anyone else. </small>"
      h2 Usage with grid#
      text You can use  inside a form. See .
      row
        text .grid
        link Grid /docs/grid
      row
        field Login
        field Password password
        button button primary
      link "Copy code" /docs/forms
      text "<form> <fieldset class=\"grid\"> <input name=\"login\" placeholder=\"Login\" aria-label=\"Login\" autocomplete=\"username\" /> <input type=\"password\" name=\"password\" placeholder=\"Password\" aria-label=\"Password\" autocomplete=\"current-password\" /> <input type=\"submit\" value=\"Log in\" /> </fieldset> </form>"
      h2 Usage with group#
      text You can use  with form elements. See .
      row
        text "role=\"group\""
        link Group /docs/group
      row
        field "Enter your email" email
        button button primary
      link "Copy code" /docs/forms
      text "<form> <fieldset role=\"group\"> <input type=\"email\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Enter your email\" autocomplete=\"email\" /> <input type=\"submit\" value=\"Subscribe\" /> </fieldset> </form>"
      link "Edit this page on GitHub" https://github.com/picocss/picocss.com/blob/main/app/routes/docs.forms._index.jsx
